{
 "content": [
  {
   "attrs": {
    "textAlign": "left"
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "The most basic of all the continuous random variables is the uniform random variable, which is equally likely to take on any value in its range (",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "\\alpha, \\beta"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": "). X is a ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "marks": [
      {
       "type": "italic"
      }
     ],
     "text": "uniform random variable",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "text": " (",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "X \\sim \\Uni(\\alpha, \\beta)"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": ") if it has PDF:",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "type": "paragraph"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "rawTex": "\\begin{aligned}\n    f(x) = \\begin{cases} \\frac{1}{\\beta - \\alpha} &\\text{when } \\alpha \\leq x \\leq \\beta \\\\ \n0 & \\text{otherwise} \\end{cases}\n\\end{aligned}"
   },
   "type": "block-tex"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "textAlign": "left"
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "Notice how the density ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "1/(\\beta - \\alpha)"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": " is exactly the same regardless of the value for x. That makes the density uniform. So why is the PDF ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "1/(\\beta - \\alpha)"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": " and not 1? That is the constant that makes it such that the integral over all possible inputs evaluates to 1.",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "type": "paragraph"
  },
  {
   "content": [
    {
     "attrs": {
      "sourceBytes": 4855,
      "sourceSha256": "ccaaa21a648a06f817c9819729d5dff973f38d8e2034f15c87ac7a86c76edef4"
     },
     "type": "interactive-demo"
    }
   ],
   "type": "borderedBox"
  },
  {
   "content": [
    {
     "attrs": {
      "textAlign": "left"
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "bold"
        }
       ],
       "text": "Example:",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "text": " You are running to the bus stop. You don’t know exactly when the bus arrives. You believe all times between 2 and 2:30 are equally likely. You show up at 2:15pm. What is P(wait < 5 minutes)?",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "textAlign": "left"
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Let ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "showEditor": false,
        "value": "T"
       },
       "type": "math_inline"
      },
      {
       "text": " be the time, in minutes after 2pm that the bus arrives. Because we think that all times are equally likely in this range, ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "showEditor": false,
        "value": "T \\sim \\Uni(\\alpha = 0, \\beta = 30)"
       },
       "type": "math_inline"
      },
      {
       "text": ". The probability that you wait 5 minutes is equal to the probability that the bus shows up between 2:15 and 2:20. In other words ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "showEditor": false,
        "value": "\\p(15 < T < 20)"
       },
       "type": "math_inline"
      },
      {
       "text": ":",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "rawTex": "\\begin{aligned}\n    \\p(\\text{Wait under 5 mins}) &= \\p(15 < T < 20) \\\\\n    &= \\int_{15}^{20} f_T(x) dx \\\\ \\\\\n    &= \\int_{15}^{20} \\frac{1}{\\beta - \\alpha} dx \\\\ \\\\\n    &= \\int_{15}^{20} \\frac{1}{30} dx \\\\ \\\\\n    &= \\frac{x}{30}\\bigg\\rvert_{15}^{20} \\\\\n    &= \\frac{20}{30} - \\frac{15}{30}  = \\frac{5}{30}\n\\end{aligned}"
     },
     "type": "block-tex"
    }
   ],
   "type": "purpleBox"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "textAlign": "left"
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "text": "We can come up with a closed form for the probability that a uniform random variable ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "X"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": " is in the range ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "a"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": " to ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "b"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": ", assuming that ",
     "type": "text"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "showEditor": false,
      "value": "\\alpha \\leq a \\leq b \\leq \\beta"
     },
     "type": "math_inline"
    },
    {
     "text": ":",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "type": "paragraph"
  },
  {
   "attrs": {
    "rawTex": "\\begin{aligned}\n    \\P(a \\leq X \\leq b) &= \\int_a^b f(x) dx \\\\\n    &= \\int_a^b \\frac{1}{\\beta - \\alpha} dx \\\\\n    &= \\frac{ b - a }{ \\beta - \\alpha }\n\\end{aligned}"
   },
   "type": "block-tex"
  }
 ],
 "type": "doc"
}
